        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Gasket material selection is one of the most critical decisions in MDV design, because the gasket must seal under pressure without swelling, hardening, or extracting materials into the formulation. The most common materials are EPDM rubber, Buna-N (nitrile), neoprene, and thermoplastic elastomers. For HFA-propelled pharmaceutical MDIs, specific elastomer grades are qualified under regulatory submissions because extractables and leachables from the gasket must meet toxicological thresholds documented in FDA and EMA guidance."
      }
