        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Dose accuracy testing for MDVs typically involves gravimetric methods — weighing the mass delivered per actuation using a precision balance — or volumetric collection into a calibrated vessel. For pharmaceutical inhalation products, dose uniformity is assessed using apparatus described in pharmacopoeial methods such as the Andersen Cascade Impactor. In industrial or consumer aerosol contexts, spray-weight tests per ASTM D5964 provide spray rate data used to infer valve consistency."
      }
