        "text": "A continuous spray valve (CSV) delivers product for as long as the actuator is depressed, with no fixed per-actuation volume. A metered dose valve, by contrast, delivers only the pre-defined volume held in its metering chamber per actuation, regardless of how long the actuator is held down. CSVs are used in household, personal care, and industrial products where variable application is acceptable. MDVs are mandatory wherever a reproducible unit dose must be guaranteed — primarily pharmaceutical aerosols and precision technical spray applications."
