                <td style="padding: 9px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">The metal disc crimped onto the aerosol can opening, housing the valve assembly</td>
                <td style="padding: 9px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">Crimp dimensions and sealing geometry per aerosol can standard</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p>The inlet and outlet gaskets operate in a precisely sequenced manner. On downstroke (actuation), the stem first closes the inlet port — isolating the metering chamber from the bulk formulation — and then opens the outlet port, allowing the metered volume to discharge through the stem orifice and actuator. On upstroke (release), the outlet closes before the inlet reopens, allowing the bulk formulation to refill the metering chamber for the next dose. This sequencing is governed entirely by the geometry of the stem and housing; there are no active control elements.</p>
      </section>

