        </div>

        <p>The EU Aerosol Dispensers Directive — available in full text at <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A31975L0324" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">EUR-Lex</a> — requires that aerosol dispensers are tested by immersion in a water bath at 50°C and that any product showing leakage fails the test. For metered dose valve assemblies, this test assesses the integrity of the complete sealing system — not merely the outlet gasket. Products showing visible bubbling, deformation, or pressure equalisation during the hot water test are rejected. This test is universally employed during filling line qualification and periodic production sampling across both consumer and pharmaceutical aerosol manufacturing.</p>
